Package: CausalMultiOmics
Title: Interpretable Causal Analysis of Multi-Block Omics Data
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Ortiz-Palma", , "ortiz9009@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Produces a quantified causal hypothesis from multi-block data
    rather than a single fitted model. Blocks of any modality (omics,
    imaging, clinical, environmental) are audited, profiled and preprocessed
    from an explicit recipe that can be replayed on a second cohort. Several
    evidence generators then run against the preprocessed data and are
    merged into one scored directed graph, in which every relationship
    records the identification strategy that would license reading it
    causally, the assumptions it rests on, how much of the data behind it
    was measured rather than imputed, whether it survives resampling, and
    what would settle it. A user-supplied causal diagram can be audited, so
    that adjusting for a mediator or a collider is reported rather than
    rewarded. Results are written as a self-contained HTML report intended
    for a reader who is not a statistician.
